// Package draw declares the bracket a composed shape's drawing sits inside:
// save the target's drawing state, and restore it afterwards, so a group's
// style reaches its children and stops at them.
//
// Each declaration is a signature with no body: the result is produced by the
// target's native implementation of the marked id, so a backend that does not
// implement one has nothing to fall back to.
//
// It used to declare a call per shape as well -- CanvasDrawCircle,
// CanvasDrawRect and five more -- from when a lowering pass read a canvas's
// children and wrote the drawing itself. A shape is an override on a platform
// primitive now (`component shapes.circle[language] { draw(@draw(e) { … }) }`),
// so what paints a circle is written in SNGL and reaches the output as that
// handler's own body. The seven were left behind: declared, emitted by
// nothing, and kept resolvable by the platforms that claim this package.
//
// These two are what the *lowering* still writes, in `canvasCall`, and they
// are the last drawing the compiler spells rather than the tree.
